{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Is one found like this.</b> Nifal pattern, and it is a past verb, as if saying: is one found in the world like this. And it is possible that the nun is a sign of the speakers: 'is one found — we — like this,' being the words of Pharaoh to his servants."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:45.224595317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}